figdown 0.1 timing
# `TIMING-LANE-ALPHABET`: the lane digits 2-9 left the closed alphabet.
# WaveDrom reads them as "value with color N" — the SAME brick as `=`,
# needing a data entry — while FigDown drew the digit as the box label
# and consumed none. Both signal lines below used to parse clean.
# The fix is `=` per data cell, named in order: x..=.=.x  data=cfg,val
timing w "retired lane digits"
signal data x..=3=5x
signal bits 01019...
